wasps                package:AA                     R Documentation

Wasps Data

Description:

     The 'wasps' data frame has 720 rows and 8 columns.

     Britta Tschanz and Sven Bacher, of the Zoological Institute at the
     University of Bern, conducted an experiment to examine the
     behaviour of a predator-prey system in relatively natural 
     conditions, with neither prey nor predators confined during
     predation.

     Three nests of the wasps were collected before the emerging phase
     and glued to the tops of insect cages.  Forty creeping thistle
     plants in a patch in a meadow were individually numbered.  Early
     on 32 days in the  summer of 2004 naturally occurring shield
     beetle larvae were removed and  replace by others placed visibly
     on randomly chosen thistle plants.   The 32 days were divided into
     eight blocks of four days, and treatments with different numbers
     of prey  and open cages were applied with 0, 1, 2, or 3 open
     cages, and with 5,  10, ..., 35 or 40 prey placed on
     randomly-chosen thistles.  At the  end of the day the plants were
     checked and the survival or not of each larva was noted; this is
     treated as a binary response.  The number of  individual wasps
     visiting the patch was estimated by extrapolation from  the number
     visiting during the peak hour just after noon, which were  caught,
     marked using dye, and released.

Usage:

     data(wasps)

Format:

     This data frame contains the following columns:

     'day' the number of days of each observation;

     'mon' the month indicator of each observation in (6-8);

     'plant' a factor variable for indicating the different plants
          (1-40);

     'cages' a factor variable for indicating the different cages
          (0-3);

     'm' the number of larvae of each observation;

     'r' a binary variable which indicates the survival or not of each
          larva (0/1);

     'w' a variable for the estimated number of wasps that visit the
          patch;

     't' the duration of each observation. 

Source:

     The data were obtained from an experiment conducted in summer of
     2004 by  Britta Tschanz and Sven Bacher of the Zoological
     Institute at the  University of Bern on the behaviour of the paper
     wasp _Polistes  dominulus_ in the presence of their prey, larvae
     of the shield beetle  _Cassida rubiginosa_.

References:

     Brazzale, A.R., Davison, A.C. and Reid, N. (2007).  _Applied 
     Asymptotics: Case Studies in Small-Sample Statistics_.  Cambridge 
     University Press, Cambridge.  Example 6.2.
